---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SEO from '../components/SEO.astro';
import { t } from '../lib/ui';

const LOCALE = 'en' as const;
---

<BaseLayout lang={LOCALE}>
  <SEO
    slot="head"
    title={`${t(LOCALE, 'about.title')} — Eduardo Kohn`}
    description="Eduardo Kohn — senior software engineer focused on Java/JVM, program analysis, software reliability, and reproducible research tooling."
    canonicalPath="/about"
    jsonLd={{ kind: 'about' }}
  />
  <article class="u-container page">
    <h1 class="page-title">{t(LOCALE, 'about.title')}</h1>
    <p>
      I'm Eduardo Kohn, a senior software engineer with more than ten years of experience building and operating
      production systems across banking, retail, consumer products, and enterprise environments. My background spans
      Java and the JVM, distributed systems, automated testing, software architecture, CI/CD, containers, and cloud
      infrastructure. I've worked across the full software lifecycle, from architecture and implementation to
      deployment, production operations, technical standards, and team leadership.
    </p>
    <p>
      Since February 2026, I have worked independently at the intersection of program analysis, software reliability,
      and reproducible research tooling. I designed and implemented the <a
        href="https://eagle-head.github.io/aquila-graph-poc/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">Aquila Graph POC</a
      >, an inspectable experiment that combines static and runtime Java facts in a provenance-preserving graph. The
      project includes reproducible workflows for execution, verification, testing, and evidence collection, grounded in
      work with JVM bytecode, control-flow and call graphs, and static/runtime identity reconciliation.
    </p>
    <p>
      My current interests include static and dynamic analysis, software testing, JVM internals, security-relevant code
      analysis, and empirical software engineering. I care about the underlying methods rather than limiting the work to
      a particular programming language. I am open to collaborating with academic and applied-research teams where
      hands-on software engineering can strengthen research tools, experiments, and infrastructure.
    </p>
    <p>
      I'm an active open-source contributor, with six merged pull requests across the <a
        href="https://github.com/phoenixframework/phoenix"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer">Phoenix framework</a
      > and <a href="https://github.com/zeek/zeek" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Zeek</a>. Four in Phoenix
      cover query-string encoding, code generation, installer crash handling, and documentation fixes; two in Zeek add
      btests for Python bytecode file signatures and error cases in expression handling. I also build and maintain
      <a href="https://github.com/eagle-head/timekeeper-countdown" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
        >timekeeper-countdown</a
      > and <a href="https://github.com/eagle-head/erli18n" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">erli18n</a>, my
      TypeScript countdown packages and pure-Erlang internationalization tooling.
    </p>
    <p>
      Before working independently, I held engineering and technical-leadership roles at Capgemini, Leroy Merlin, AB
      InBev, EY, Livelo Brasil, Semantix Brasil, and Hubchain Technologies. Across those roles, I developed Java and
      Spring Boot services, React and TypeScript interfaces, and React Native applications; worked with relational and
      NoSQL databases, Kafka, Docker, Kubernetes, and AWS; and helped establish architecture, testing, accessibility,
      delivery, and design-system standards.
    </p>
    <p>
      I am pursuing a Bachelor's degree in Computer Science at Universidade São Judas Tadeu (2024–2028) and hold a
      Bachelor's degree in Business Administration from UNISBA (2003–2007). I am based in Ashland, Ohio, United States.
    </p>
    <p>
      This blog is where I think in public, writing as I work through program analysis, software reliability,
      distributed systems, networking, performance, testing, and production software internals. <a href="/papers"
        >Papers</a
      > are longer pieces developed with scientific rigour; <a href="/posts">Posts</a> are shorter notes that share an idea
      while it is still taking shape.
    </p>
    <p>
      Find me on <a href="https://github.com/eagle-head" target="_blank" rel="me noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>,
      <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/eduardokohn84" target="_blank" rel="me noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn</a>, or
      subscribe to the <a href="/newsletter">newsletter</a> to get new pieces by email.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page {
    --measure: var(--measure-paper);
    padding-block: var(--space-6);
  }
  .page-title {
    font-size: var(--text-2xl);
    font-weight: var(--font-weight-extrabold);
    letter-spacing: var(--tracking-tight);
    line-height: var(--leading-tight);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-5) 0;
    color: var(--color-fg);
  }
  .page p {
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    line-height: var(--leading-relaxed);
    color: var(--color-text);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-4) 0;
  }
</style>
